        "reasoning_content": "You are a rater applying idea-evaluation instrument...\n\nWe need rate proposal P1305.\n\nProposal: Post-Market Log Surveillance Dashboard. internal operations tool ingests lifetime logs... flags anomalies relevant to Article 72 post-market monitoring and Article 26(5)... dedicated compliance-operations team builds querying interface on top of lab's logging infrastructure, setting threshold alerts... generating periodic monitoring reports... Continuous surveillance converts passive logs into active compliance evidence...\n\nWe need six subscales.\n\nparadigm_relatedness (1-4):\n4 = paradigm breaking: introduces new elements AND changes relationship between lab's R&D and compliance obligations, or addresses larger problem of what lab researches\n3 = paradigm stretching: changes that relationship (e.g., logging woven into science, new partners or offerings born from compliance)\n2 = slightly paradigm stretching: introduces new elements (tools, formats, processes) but still treats compliance as logging practice\n1 = paradigm preserving: standard compliance and logging practice; lab's way of working unchanged\n\nProposal is dashboard for logs. Introduces tool but still treats compliance as logging practice. It's slightly paradigm stretching? It introduces new elements tools, formats, processes but still treats compliance as logging practice. So 2.\n\nOriginality (1-4):\n4 not expressed before AND ingenious...\n3 unusual interesting shows some imagination\n2 interesting\n1 common mundane boring\n\nDashboard for logs is common, mundane. Probably 1 = common, mundane, boring. Could be 2? Ingesting logs and flagging anomalies is fairly standard compliance ops. I'd say common. So 1.\n\nApplicability (1-4):\n4 solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, Y part of stated problem)\n3 solves implied problem related...\n2 may have some benefit within special situation...\n1 intervention not stated...\n\nStated problem: