nreasonable or unlikely to solve problem. Could be 2.\n\nOriginality evidence: A public, containerized test harness for log fidelity under privacy constraints is unusual in AI compliance practice and shows imagination. Score 3.\n\nParadigm_relatedness evidence: The lab would turn a compliance logging obligation into an open scientific measurement product and community standard, weaving logging into research output. Score 3.\n\nImplementability evidence: Developing metrics, containerized harnesses and validation against three model families requires dedicated engineering effort but is feasible with existing R&D skills. Score 3.\n\nAcceptability evidence: Publishing an open benchmark for regulatory traceability aligns with scientific norms and raises no legal or political concerns. Score 4.\n\nReturn.\n\nEnsure integer levels.\n\nFinal output JSON? Probably plain text. Provide as requested.\n\nLet's deliver.",
