ient-facing monitoring service born from mandatory logging, thereby changing the lab’s relationship with compliance obligations. Score 3.\n\nOriginality_evidence: Turning required logs into a hosted analytics product for both internal and external use is unusual and shows imagination beyond standard internal logging. Score 3.\n\nAcceptability_evidence: Offering dashboards for post-market monitoring aligns with regulatory expectations and does not violate legal or business norms. Score 4.\n\nImplementability_evidence: Building a streaming ingestion pipeline, hosted platform and alerting requires data engineering and compliance resources beyond routine logging. Score 3? Might be 2? Let's keep 3 = some changes reasonably feasible.\n\nApplicability_evidence: The dashboard directly supports the mandated post-market monitoring under Article 72 and operational oversight under Article 26(5) required by the logging mandate. Score 4.\n\nEffectiveness_evidence: It will help use and interpret logs but does not itself ensure automatic event recording or the specific content required by Article 12. Score 3.\n\nReturn JSON? Instruction says return rating echoing id exactly. Probably plain lines.\n\nI'll output structured.\n\n",
