ve stated problem without regard for workability (if you could do it, it would solve main problem). Does this solve logging mandate? It builds ingestion pipeline and retention store, which meets logging. Also adapts R&D. So yes solves. Might be partial? It meets logging mandate and uses data. Probably 4.\n\nEvidence: The observatory directly satisfies Article 12 automatic recording and traceability while repurposing logs for R&D.\n\napplicability: degree clearly applies to stated problem. 4 = solves identified problem directly related to stated problem (do X to get Y, and Y is part of stated problem). Yes. So 4.\n\nEvidence: Building a log ingestion platform directly addresses the mandate to technically allow automatic recording over lifetime.\n\nReturn JSON? Probably list. Instruction: For each subscale give \"<subscale>_evidence\" first then \"<subscale>\". Return rating echoing id exactly.\n\nWe'll output structured.\n\nLet's produce:\n\nid: P1242\nacceptability_evidence: ...\nacceptability:4 etc.\n\nMake sure order: acceptability, implementability, paradigm_relatedness, originality, effectiveness, applicability\n\nProvide one sentence evidence each.\n\n",
